# Normalize line endings so diffs stay clean across Windows/Linux/macOS.
# Text files are stored LF in the repository and checked out LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The frozen Command Center planning pack is a CHECKSUMMED artifact, and the
# rule above was wrong for it. `* text=auto eol=lf` normalized eight CRLF
# files to LF on the way in, so their bytes stopped matching the SHA-256
# lines in `command center/MANIFEST.txt` — which hashes the pack as
# delivered. `scripts/build_context_pack.py` verifies that manifest on every
# run, so a fresh clone reported a broken frozen pack. The working tree only
# looked fine because the original files sat there undisturbed; the first
# `git checkout` materialised them as LF and the check went red.
#
# `-text` means no conversion in either direction: what was committed is what
# is checked out. Scoped to this directory because that is exactly the unit
# the manifest covers — every path here is verified by it, and no path
# outside it is. Line-ending normalization stays the default everywhere else.
#
# QUOTED because the directory name contains a space. Unquoted, git splits on
# it and reads `center/**` as an attribute name — `.gitattributes:18: not a
# valid attribute name` — leaving the pattern inert while looking correct.
# `whitespace=-trailing-space` rides along for the same paths: with `-text`,
# git sees each preserved CR as trailing whitespace and `git diff --check`
# flags every line of every CRLF file. This repo runs that check at each gate,
# so without it the fix trades a red context pack for a permanently noisy
# whitespace check. It suppresses only that class, only here.
"command center/**" -text whitespace=-trailing-space

# Binary files: never touch these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
